hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16818","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Abu Musa al-Anazi Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Ibn Awn from Kulthum ibn Jabr, he said: We were at Wasit al-Qasab with Abd al-A'la ibn Abd Allah ibn Amir, he said: And there was with him a man called Abu al-Ghadiya; he asked for water to drink and was brought a silver-plated vessel, and he refused to drink, and he mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned this hadith: Do not return after me as disbelievers, or as misguided ones, Ibn Abi Adi was uncertain, some of you striking the necks of others. And there was a man reviling so-and-so, and I said: By Allah, if Allah enables me against you in a battle. And when the day of Siffin came, I suddenly saw him wearing a coat of mail, he said: And I noticed the opening at the neck-hole of the coat of mail, and I stabbed him and killed him, and he turned out to be Ammar ibn Yasir. He said: I said: And what hand withheld them, that he dislikes drinking from a silver-plated vessel though he had killed Ammar ibn Yasir?"
"16819","He said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Rabi'a ibn Kulthum narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Abu Ghadiya al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the day of al-Aqaba and said: O people, your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you until you meet your Lord, like the sanctity of this day of yours in this land of yours in this month of yours. Shall I not have conveyed? They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, have I conveyed?"
"16820","Affan narrated to us, he said: Rabi'a narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Ghadiya al-Juhani say: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Aqaba, and he said: O people, your blood, and he mentioned the like of it."
"16821","He said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, he said: I heard al-As ibn Amr al-Tufawi say: Abu al-Ghadiya and Habib ibn al-Harith and the mother of Abu al-Aliya went out as emigrants to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they accepted Islam, and the woman said: Advise me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Beware of what offends the ear."
